            <ArticleTitle>Intracanal medications and antibiotics in the control of interappointment flare-ups.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>997-1005</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute exacerbation of symptoms, or &quot;flare-up,&quot; after the debridement of the root canals and provisional restoration is a well-known postoperative complication of endodontic treatment. In this clinical study, various types of intracanal medications were compared for their ability to decrease interappointment flare-ups. The result showed that use of intracanal medicaments containing anti-inflammatory agents in combination with the administration of prophylactic systematic antibiotics was the most effective method of controlling interappointment flare-ups.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
